  "description": "Proposed work is for the installation of two new pairs of sash windows into existing box sash frames, and one new pair of French casement leaves into an casement frame.  The sash windows are on the front and casement leaves are on the rear side return, all at basement (lower ground floor) level.  New sashes and casement leaves will match the current windows, made from timber with traditional moulding profiles and glass sightlines.  They will be painted in white semi-gloss water based micro-porus paint.  Glass will be clear double glazed heritage slimline units with dry seal externally.  Sashes will be cord hung opening top and bottom, casement leaves will be side hung opening out.  Existing box frames and casement frames will be retained and repaired as required.  No work or modifications to the internal reveals or external brick reveals, structural openings or fabric of the building. ",
  "subdivision_of_building": "Basement flat 1 only.  Works to the front and rear-side elevations only.  The proposal covers only the opening parts of the windows.  The window frames, reveals and structural openings will not be changed or disrupted.",
